Z||000023||Seanh||01-01-2001||02:36 PM||||This is going to sound stupid, but last year I had to do a research paper on when the Millenium should really end. Turns out, to no big suprise, the completion of 2000 years was late nite/this morning. Although, now (like newborns) start with zero, the number "0" zero was not "invented" at the time they started keeping track of years, so they started with 1. And, there was no compensation for it later, therefore making the millenium end last night. Sorry to be the odd one of the bunch, but thats really how it is.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000024||Raydar||01-01-2001||07:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>well, I don't want to get into a debate about this.. heh.. but I celebrated the millennium last year, whether it was technically the millennium change or not. (cause last year was when all the huge parties were, not this year!)<P>anyway, happy new years..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Glad that YOU got to celebrate, last year. Several of us had to babysit the !$@%&!$ computers. <BR>I even got to FIX one. Not even my dept.,  but I was the only one in the building who knew anything about it. <BR>And for the people who said that the Y2K bug was just hype... Nope. Not at all. This was one that had gotten overlooked. At midnight, it dropped like a rock. All the preparations <I>were</I> worth it.<P>This year? Went to visit some friends. Didn't drink a drop. (Dammit.) Had a good time anyway, and woke up with no hangover.<P>Happy New Year to all!<P><BR>  ||||reg||1
