Z||000026||Jimmy||01-02-2001||03:08 AM||||If you believe or follow the Christian/Gregorian calendar The new Decades/Centurys/Melleniums start on the 1's.  There really is no arguing it as this is just a matter of fact.  Go back 100 years, people were not confused then.  Newspapers didn't write anything but "happy new year" in 1900, but if you look at 1901 newspaper said "welcome to the new century".  Zeros are just more fun and thats why 2000 was a great marketing hit.  The reasoning of decades in accordance to birthdays is flawed as you start at the age of zero not 1.<P>Happy New Mellenium/Century/New Year!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Jim||||reg||1
