Z||000033||Monkeyman||01-03-2001||04:39 AM||||Hugh--99 years from now will be the turn of the century, not the start of another new millenium.  That's more like 999 years from now (or 1000 years from now depending on which way you're looking at it).  BTW--Unless  I'm wrong (I'm sure I'll hear about it if I am), last Monday was officially the start of the new century, too (not last year).  A century is either 100 years or a big, ugly Buick.  If you were born on January 1st (the day the calendar started) you would be one year old on Jan, 1 in the year 0001.  Therefore, the previous 100 years ended on Jan 1, 2001.||||reg||1
