Z||000035||Will||01-03-2001||09:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jimmy:<BR><B>If you believe or follow the Christian/Gregorian calendar The new Decades/Centurys/Melleniums start on the 1's.  There really is no arguing it as this is just a matter of fact.  Go back 100 years, people were not confused then.  Newspapers didn't write anything but "happy new year" in 1900, but if you look at 1901 newspaper said "welcome to the new century".  Zeros are just more fun and thats why 2000 was a great marketing hit.  The reasoning of decades in accordance to birthdays is flawed as you start at the age of zero not 1.<P>Happy New Mellenium/Century/New Year!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Jim</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Did you celebrate your 0th birthday?<BR>You (your parents at least) celebrate your first birthday at the completion of your first year. Before you celebrate your first birthday, you are in your first year. The calendar works the same way. 2001 starts the third millenium, just like <B>19</B>01 started the <B>20th</B> century.||||reg||1
